-    // originals: the copy was taken before any DXE allocation could
-    // scribble over the freshly landed window, so it is the earliest
-    // surviving witness of the previous boot's write. A missing copy
-    // counts as k == 0. The window originals are still scanned for
-    // the out-of-sequence anomaly (a slot past slot 0 holding its own
-    // magic), and window slot 0 remains the arm branch's write
-    // target -- next boot's BootShim copies from there. Branch
-    // semantics are unchanged from M3J: k == 0 arms and resets,
-    // k == 1 draws SURVIVED and writes nothing, ODD never resets.
